### Justification
Official Indian government data reveals that India's imports from China actually declined by 27.63% during the April-August 2020 period compared to the previous year, directly contradicting assertions of an import growth. According to statistics presented to the Lok Sabha by Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal and reported by [Business Today](https://www.businesstoday.in/current/economy-politics/imports-from-china-decline-by-27-63-during-april-august-2020-piyush-goyal/story/416674.html), the total import value fell to $21.58 billion. Although there was a temporary uptick in imports of Chinese medical supplies and electronic gadgets following record lows in April and May 2020 as detailed by [Drishti IAS](https://www.drishtiias.com/daily-updates/daily-news-analysis/rising-imports-from-china), the overall figure for the five-month period represents a significant decrease, refuting any claims of an increase.